            <ArticleTitle>[Use of a balloon-tipped guidewire to pre-dilate coronary stenosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of coronary angioplasty of very tight stenoses are reported in which, after failure of conventional low-profile catheters, a balloon-tipped guidewire was used to predilate the lesion, with subsequent advancement of a larger balloon catheter over the wire itself to complete the dilatation. It is suggested that this balloon-tipped guidewire can be helpful for safe predilatation of very tight coronary stenoses with no need for complex catheter exchanges.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
